use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/FormParticipation import FormParticipation

export ui-component Checkbox:
    description:
        A checkbox is a box the user ticks or unticks. It can also show a third
        "partly checked" state, such as a "select all" box when only some of
        the items under it are ticked.

    behaviors:
        - @{FormParticipation}

    states:
        Checked, unchecked, or partly checked. Only the component using the
        checkbox can set it to partly checked; the user never can. Clicking a
        partly checked box makes it checked.

    label:
        A checkbox has a name saying what it controls, usually shown as a label
        next to it. Clicking the label works the same as clicking the box.

    activation:
        The user ticks it the usual way for the platform: clicking, tapping, or
        using the keyboard. Which keys do this is up to the chosen library.

    disabled:
        A disabled checkbox can't be changed, and it's clear to the user that
        it's unavailable. It keeps showing its current state. A read-only
        checkbox can be focused and read out, but not changed.

    submission:
        In a form, a ticked checkbox sends its value, which the component can
        choose, and an unticked one sends nothing. Whether a partly checked box
        sends its value is up to the chosen library. A required checkbox, such
        as agreeing to terms, must be ticked before the form can be submitted.

    independence:
        Each checkbox is its own yes-or-no choice. Ticking one never unticks
        another. Choices where only one can be picked are a RadioGroup.

    nonGoals:
        - Not meant for settings that take effect the moment they're changed.
            That's usually a Switch. A checkbox is usually part of a form that
            is saved later
